1902–03 was the 15th season of competitive football for [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]], who competed in the [[Scottish First Division]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1900/celtic1903.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1902-03|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> For the third season in a row, Celtic failed to add major honours to their tally as they finished 5th in the league and were eliminated from the Scottish Cup in the 3rd round following a 0-3 home defeat to [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]].

This was the last season at the club for captain [[Sandy McMahon]], who would briefly play for fellow Glasgow club [[Partick Thistle F.C.|Partick Thistle]] before retiring.

Celtic won the [[Glasgow Charity Cup]].

